- What monitoring dashboards and alerting thresholds would you set for p99 across components?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests edge caching behavior, tail latency, and backpressure under regional surge—a practical beginner scenario for performance testing.

## Key Concepts
- Edge caching and cache warming
- Tail latency (p95/p99)
- API gateway backpressure and circuit breakers
- Regional autoscaling and cost/latency trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
import http from 'k6/http';
import { sleep } from 'k6';
export let options = {
  scenarios: {
    regionalSurge: { executor: 'ramping-vus', startVUs: 0, stages: [ { duration: '2m', target: 50 }, { duration: '8m', target: 200 } ] }
  }
};
export default function () {
  http.get('https://region-A.example.com/pricing');
  http.post('https://region-A.example.com/book', JSON.stringify({}), { headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' } });
  sleep(0.5);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would network jitter influence your test results and how would you compensate for it?
- What signals would you use to decide if the edge cache warming was successful?

## Why This Is Asked

To assess how candidates craft end-to-end performance tests for ultra-low-latency pipelines with multiple services and external dependencies, ensuring backpressure, fail-fast behavior, and autoscaling.

## Key Concepts

- End-to-end and tail latency
- Bounded buffers, backpressure
- Circuit breakers and fail-fast
- Traffic shaping and ramp-up
- Observability and tracing (OpenTelemetry, Jaeger)
- Kubernetes autoscaling (HPA, KEDA optional)

## Code Example

```javascript
import http from 'k6/http';
import { check, sleep } from 'k6';
export let options = { vus: 1000, duration: '60s' };
export default function () {
  const r = http.post('https://ads.example.com/bid', JSON.stringify({bid: 1}), { headers: { 'Content-Type':'application/json' }});
  check(r, { 'status 200': (r)=> r.status===200 });
  sleep(0.0005);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure and isolate downstream latency vs upstream latency in a live campaign?
- How would you simulate upstream outages without affecting other tenants in a shared cluster?

